notes:
•  NEW: PTZ panel, docked in the lower left under Video Sources (like MxControlCenter). It works on the active tile (click a tile):
     - Camera vPTZ: the camera itself zooms into its picture and moves the view - MOBOTIX's virtual PTZ, the same as the Zoom and Pan buttons in the camera's web page. Everyone watching that camera sees the change; recordings normally keep the full picture.
     - In MxScout: only that tile's picture is zoomed (up to 8x) and moved - nothing changes on the camera; works for every camera and in playback. A ZOOM badge with a small map shows where you are; drag the picture to move around.
     - arrow pad (click for a step, hold to keep moving), centre, Zoom + / Zoom -, 1x, speed slider;
     - 6 presets per camera: click to go, right-click to save the current view;
     - mouse wheel over a tile zooms (In MxScout: around the spot under the mouse);
     - optional: click in the picture to centre the view there;
     - ⇄ button: if left/right go the wrong way on a camera, swap them (remembered per camera).
     Click the PTZ bar to fold the panel away; it remembers.
